WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.595
Welcome to 687 Starflower Lane.

2
00:00:03.645 --> 00:00:09.467
It's a 2024 custom ranch on just over five wooded acres, backing right onto state forest.

3
00:00:09.517 --> 00:00:14.548
On the left is the forty by fifty heated garage, and on the right, the house.

4
00:00:14.598 --> 00:00:19.496
Come on in, and let's walk through it the way we're planning to live in it.

5
00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:26.042
Through the front door, the foyer opens straight into the main living space.

6
00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:30.786
Dark wood floors run through the whole main level, with white trim and black windows.

7
00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:38.593
This is the great room, about twenty-one by nineteen feet, and it's going to be our piano lounge.

8
00:00:38.643 --> 00:00:44.435
The grand piano is the centerpiece, keys toward the kitchen, with the lid opening toward the fireplace.

9
00:00:44.485 --> 00:00:52.434
Across the hearth, two black leather cigar chairs face each other over a tufted leather bench, with the carved mirror panel above the mantel.

10
00:00:52.484 --> 00:00:54.249
And look up: a coffered ceiling.

11
00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:00.794
Through the wide cased opening is the dining room, with a table for six.

12
00:01:00.844 --> 00:01:05.219
The ten-foot glass doors open right out to the covered back deck and the hot tub.

13
00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:11.137
The kitchen wraps around a big island with four counter stools.

14
00:01:11.187 --> 00:01:16.820
White shaker cabinets, stone counters, and a long window over the sink, looking out into the trees.

15
00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:25.196
Around the corner is the mudroom hall, with the door in from the garage, plus the pantry and a half bath.

16
00:01:25.246 --> 00:01:29.073
So coming in from the car or the gym stays out of the living space.

17
00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:35.231
Back past the great room, a short hall leads to the primary suite.

18
00:01:35.281 --> 00:01:42.603
The bedroom is seventeen by eighteen feet, with the king bed on the back wall, a nightstand on each side, and two tall chests.

19
00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:50.223
Off the bedroom, there's a walk-in closet that's more than ten by thirteen feet.

20
00:01:50.273 --> 00:01:55.678
And the ensuite has a soaking tub under the window, a long double vanity, and a glass shower.

21
00:01:55.728 --> 00:01:58.670
The laundry room is right next door, off the foyer.

22
00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.479
Now let's head downstairs.

23
00:02:02.529 --> 00:02:05.150
Fifteen steps take us down to the lower level.

24
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.747
The family room is about twenty-one by twenty-two feet.

25
00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:21.598
Our gray L-shaped sectional, fourteen feet by ten and a half, wraps the corner and faces the seventy-five inch TV on a white media console, with a square coffee table in the middle.

26
00:02:21.648 --> 00:02:24.116
And over in the corner, the massage chair.

27
00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:28.003
Now for the fun part.

28
00:02:28.053 --> 00:02:30.428
That bookcase is actually a hinged door.

29
00:02:30.478 --> 00:02:42.430
Behind it is the speakeasy: the original burnt-orange walls, a deep red rug, a high-top table with four counter chairs under a low brass pendant, and an oak and marble bar cart against the far wall.

30
00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:55.339
Back out in the hall, there's a full bath, and then bedroom two, the kids' room, with a navy tufted full bed, a nightstand, a dresser, and a desk with a white chair.

31
00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:05.346
Across the hall, bedroom three is the teen room, and later the guest room, with a queen sleigh bed, a dresser, and a small desk.

32
00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:11.865
The rest of the lower level stays unfinished, for storage and utilities.

33
00:03:11.915 --> 00:03:19.123
In the open west corner there's a simple office: a glass desk and task chair, with cube shelving and a curtain to define it.

34
00:03:19.173 --> 00:03:23.689
The furnace, water heater, and well equipment all stay open and easy to reach.

35
00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:29.320
From there, a stair goes straight up into the garage.

36
00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:40.487
And right at the top is the recovery corner: the cold plunge, a thirty-inch wet mat, and then the glass door of the three-person infrared sauna, with a red light therapy panel built into the door.

37
00:03:40.537 --> 00:03:42.653
One step from the cold, into the heat.

38
00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:51.111
The gym fills the back half of the garage, on black rubber mats.

39
00:03:51.161 --> 00:03:59.777
An eight by eight lifting platform and a four-post rig sit under the thirteen-foot center of the vaulted ceiling, with rings and a climbing rope overhead.

40
00:03:59.827 --> 00:04:08.330
Dumbbells, bumper plates, a barbell tree, and plyo boxes line the back wall, with the reverse hyper and the glute-ham developer tucked behind the sauna.

41
00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:20.896
On the far side, there's a stretch and TV corner with a futon, a spin bike and an air bike, a curved treadmill and a ski-row machine, and a small standing-desk office at the back window.

42
00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.994
And up front, three bays, all parked nose-in.

43
00:04:31.044 --> 00:04:32.392
On the left, the SUV.

44
00:04:32.442 --> 00:04:35.785
In the center, the camper van, under the tall door.

45
00:04:35.835 --> 00:04:42.106
And on the right, a four-post lift, with the sports car up top and the electric SUV underneath.

46
00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:57.117
That's 687 Starflower: a piano lounge on the main floor, a movie room and speakeasy downstairs, and a full gym with a recovery corner in the garage.

47
00:04:57.167 --> 00:04:59.476
Thanks for walking through it with us.
